{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015611-spell-casting-and-the-inspired-condition-infinite-loop-question","id":1015611,"title":"Spell casting and the Inspired Condition infinite loop question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-11T02:12:13-08:00","id":1015611,"title":"Spell casting and the Inspired Condition infinite loop question","content":"I have noticed that a player is using a loop to gain Arcane beats whenever he needs them. He isn't doing this for every spell he casts, but often enough where I have noticed it happening within every scene of any significant length.<br /> <br /> He originally got an exceptional success on some spell-casting dice roll. I forget which one. Now he has an infinite loop going where he constantly has the Inspired Condition, and uses it to gain an exceptional success on dice rolls he is good at. Gaining three successes isn't that hard, because the skills he uses have a large dice pool. And, if he runs out of exceptional successes then he uses the Mind 4 Intuitive Leap attainment to gain an exceptional success, which he uses to gain the Inspired Condition on whatever he wants. And it's not unreasonable stuff. It is always at least somewhat related to what is going on. Like Inspired Condition(Time-magic), because he just got an exceptional success on a Time-spell.<br /> <br /> So, I'm just asking: is this infinite loop working as intended? It seems to me that there's nothing in the books that says it doesn't work like this.<br /> <br /> I don't have a huge problem with it, but I have heard grumblings from other players, because they can't get arcane beats whenever they want. Should I just teach this technique to everyone, so everyone can have the Inspired Condition all the time?<br /> <br /> I should probably have another read through how Conditions are supposed to work, because what's bugging me is that the Condition system isn't being used to fuel the story in any way. It is being used to quickly advance in Arcane Experience. And it's my understanding that that's not the intended use of the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","user":"TelperionST","date":". 12-11-2016, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:28:43-08:00","id":1015616,"title":"","content":"It is viable to give yourself conditions to learn from the experience. It is listed that some initiates are given such conditions from their mentor to help them grow as mages. <br /> <br /> In truth, this seems to be more an issue among players. In any game there is a gentleman's agreement so I suggest taking to your player. There are some cases of something being in the rules that you can do but that doesn't always mean you should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:29:17-08:00","id":1015617,"title":"","content":"Within the game I could reasonably say that the character has become so accustomed to gaining exceptional successes that they no longer inspire him. Gaining an exceptional success has become what he expects of himself, and therefore it is not exceptional. It is the base-line success that he expects of himself, and is therefore not worthy of the Inspired Condition.<br /> <br /> However, I don't want to punish a player just because he has figured something out. Found a way to gain an advantage. At the same time there's a constant nagging feeling: is this working as intended? It feels broken, but I can't point to a rule in the rulebook that says &quot;this is why it's broken&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T03:11:16-08:00","id":1015624,"title":"","content":"First, if the other players are grumbling, it might be worth pointing towards their Praxis spells (they should all have at least one). The whole point of having some Praxis spells is to, well, not have to waste time on this. You can just pick a few spells that are always 3 success for an exceptional success without even getting into Conditions. If they're not harvesting Arcane Beats from that... they're kind of missing out.<br /> <br /> I think it's also worth not handing out Inspired for every exceptional success. Inspired isn't the only positive Condition out there. As well, exceptional successes can result in other characters gaining a Condition that's favorable towards the original character. The exceptional success rules for spell casting say the player can choose, &quot;A Condition which will give Arcane Beats when resolved, on either the mage or her subject.&quot; So don't feel bound to have it always be Inspired, or always on the caster. <br /> <br /> Honestly, it's not broken because trying to get exceptional successes for Arcane Beats is something you're supposed to do, to the point where this method isn't even necessary. However, Beats are supposed to be moments of narrative significance, and if they're just becoming boring check marks that's not how it's supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T03:19:55-08:00","id":1015628,"title":"","content":"Here's another question:<br /> <br /> The Inspired Condition doesn't allow you to gain beats.<br /> <br /> If you take the Inspired Condition with the exceptional success from a spell-casting dice roll then does that overwrite the &quot;you don't get beats for completing this condition&quot; part of Inspired Condition?<br /> <br /> The players haven't really figured out how Praxis work, and apparently I haven't thought of everything either. Well, it's my first time running Mage 2E, so I'm still learning stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T03:25:31-08:00","id":1015629,"title":"","content":"We agreed at the table that you can't get a positive condition from using a positive condition - with some exceptions judged by ST and players. So when using condition that lets you change success into exceptional success you don't get another condition. It declutters the game and everything goes smoother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T03:35:25-08:00","id":1015631,"title":"","content":"Okay, I had another round of discussions with the players, and the whole situation seems to be resolved. I'm going to be helping those players who aren't quite so intimately familiar with the system to gain more Arcane Beats. Thanks for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T03:55:37-08:00","id":1015634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015611-spell-casting-and-the-inspired-condition-infinite-loop-question?p=1015628#post1015628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inspired Condition doesn't allow you to gain beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, it lets you gain willpower. It's still useful, but not in the xp department. At least, that's how I play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T05:43:56-08:00","id":1015648,"title":"","content":"You gain beats from Inspired because you resolve it. Like almost all Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:21:45-08:00","id":1015722,"title":"","content":"Consider using group beats if one player is gaining way more than everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:37:08-08:00","id":1015729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015611-spell-casting-and-the-inspired-condition-infinite-loop-question?p=1015628#post1015628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another question:<br /> <br /> The Inspired Condition doesn't allow you to gain beats.<br /> <br /> If you take the Inspired Condition with the exceptional success from a spell-casting dice roll then does that overwrite the &amp;quot;you don't get beats for completing this condition&amp;quot; part of Inspired Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what &quot;Beat: N/A&quot; means. You always gain a Beat for resolving a Condition, unless the Condition explicitly says otherwise, and Inspired does not. The Beat criteria provides a way of getting Beats out of Persistent Conditions without resolving them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015611-spell-casting-and-the-inspired-condition-infinite-loop-question?p=1015628#post1015628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The players haven't really figured out how Praxis work, and apparently I haven't thought of everything either. Well, it's my first time running Mage 2E, so I'm still learning stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>They work just like any other spell, except that when you cast a spell as a Praxis it gains an exceptional success on three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> Anyway, what your player is doing with using Inspired to get Exceptional Successes more easily and using Exceptional Successes to gain Inspired is completely legit by the rules, but if it's causing a problem for the group you should discuss it with your players. Which it sounds like you've done and worked something out, so glad to hear things are going well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T03:49:40-08:00","id":1016048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015611-spell-casting-and-the-inspired-condition-infinite-loop-question?p=1015729#post1015729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what &quot;Beat: N/A&quot; means. You always gain a Beat for resolving a Condition, unless the Condition explicitly says otherwise, and Inspired does not. The Beat criteria provides a way of getting Beats out of Persistent Conditions without resolving them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I see. I wish the book was more clear about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T05:01:31-08:00","id":1016062,"title":"","content":"It's written in the Character Advancement section in the list of ways to gain beats on page 81, as well as in the text describing how Conditions work on page 230. I realize it's easy to skim through and miss things in RPG books just because it's so much text to go through just to play the game (I'm a repeat offender of that myself) but the book really is quite clear when it spells it out in both relevant parts of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T08:44:06-08:00","id":1016116,"title":"","content":"I think the best solution to this is to use Group Beats. Unless you have a problem with this rapid advancement, in which case houserule it, pool it. That way, players have incentive to cooperate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T09:06:56-08:00","id":1016131,"title":"","content":"Or simply don't allow your players to pick the Conditions they get for an Exceptional Success (Assuming talking to the player(s) didn't work), or skip the Condition and give them a Beat. I do the latter at my table.<br /> <br /> Typically though Conditions don't affect spellcasting without magical intervention so it'd also be simple enough to just let them take the Inspired Condition and then let them know that won't affect a spell casting roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-12-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:37:44-08:00","id":1016684,"title":"","content":"I resolved the situation by simply putting up a list of every way the book says you can gain regular and arcane beats. From now on everyone should have a much better way of when to ask for beats, how to get them and what to do to set themselves up for beats. I don't have a problem with rapid character progression, but I was simply unaware of some of the details up until now. I really do try to run the game as the rules are written, but there are a lot of little bits that I haven't noticed or understood quite right.<br /> <br /> For example, this week I noticed that little bit of text in the Magic section that explains what the Order Rotes on the character sheet do. They give a +1 to spellcasting dice rolls on a Rote on some skills. I keep reading the rules over and over again, and every time there's usually some individual sentence that I honestly thought that I had read properly, but apparently I had just skimmed it. So, with a game as complex as this one it's a lot of reading the pages over and over again. I don't mind. I just don't get things right the first time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:09:50-08:00","id":1017127,"title":"","content":"I bought the Condition cards and I'm thinking of having a rule that you can't get a Condition on a card that someone else already has until they resolve it and give me back the card. I'm not sure if this will slow things down a little or not...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T21:22:29-08:00","id":1017483,"title":"","content":"Glad you found a solution, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2648_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2648\" data-vbnamecard=\"2648\">TelperionST</a> -- if you don't mind my asking, how often do you ask for rolls? About how many beats per session are folks earning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T06:46:50-08:00","id":1018440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015611-spell-casting-and-the-inspired-condition-infinite-loop-question?p=1017483#post1017483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you don't mind my asking, how often do you ask for rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rolls on anything approximating significant are very common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015611-spell-casting-and-the-inspired-condition-infinite-loop-question?p=1017483#post1017483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> About how many beats per session are folks earning?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the regular biweekly gaming group they get 5-6 beats (regular and arcane) per session. A common session lasts for three scenes.<br /> For the daily PbP group they get maybe 3-4 beats per scene.<br /> The disparaty between groups is the from the different medium of play: there are longer conversations and debates going on in the real-time game than in the PbP game. The PbP game is more gamist in that respect, which doesn't bother me in the least.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:31:26-08:00","id":1023232,"title":"","content":"Simple fix? If it's not dramatic don't roll dice. He can't shed the condition, he can't keep the loop going.<br /> <br /> Also? Conditions that aren't Persistent last for a scene. They are shed if not resolved within them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:42:40-08:00","id":1023243,"title":"","content":"No they're not. Persistent only means the Condition is hard to get rid of and tend to be a lot harder to resolve.<br /> Normal Conditions disappear through four methods: Resolving them, letting them expire (when they do is written in the Condition text in those cases), removing them with a spell, and ST telling the player that the Condition is no longer relevant.<br /> There's nothing in the rules about Conditions only lasting for a scene. If that were the case the book wouldn't have rules for removing conditions that are no longer relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:58:30-08:00","id":1023249,"title":"","content":"Its been mentioned before that most non-Persistant Conditions do expire after a scene. I don't think its a hard rule, but its a good rule of thumb to follow. If you gained Inspired in one scene, and you don't use it, by the next scene its well within the ST's rights to say that you're no longer as inspired/Inspired as you were. <br /> <br /> I like to think that Conditions of the non-persistant variety are generally meant to have immediate narrative impact, not XP farming mentalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:21:36-08:00","id":1023259,"title":"","content":"That would be using the fourth method I described, but reading the book I get the impression it should be a rare occurrence and not something that happens after most scenes. (In my group we generally gain several conditions each scene and rarely use up all of them during that particular scene.)<br /> Top of page 231: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">We recommend doing this sparingly</span></span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:02:58-08:00","id":1023282,"title":"","content":"And I'm saying that &quot;scene-end&quot; and &quot;no longer relevant&quot; have a high instance of being the same thing for a lot of Conditions. Especially ones generated through Dramatic Failures or Exceptional Successes, which is the case being discussed here. Scenes end when all the action is generally resolved, and moving on to a new series of actions. Generally speaking, what Inspired/Shook/etc you previously has worn off, the adrenaline has faded. These kinds of Conditions are generally meant to be used and Resolved kind of immediately, doing something almost right away.<br /> <br /> Now, Conditions that come from something more serious, such as a breaking point, will often have longer durations because these are generally long term implications on a person. Magically created Conditions will last as long as the magic power say they do, because magic. These are generally the only time when a Condition will come with a pre-listed expiration date. But Conditions generated through general dice rolls aren't generally a big-impact-situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:44:57-08:00","id":1023296,"title":"","content":"While you can certainly choose to run things that way, there's nothing in the books that affirms that approach. That's not, &quot;how the rules are meant to be used,&quot; just how some people feel is the best way to use them to maximum effect. The books never say to treat getting a given Condition from an exceptional success on a normal roll vs. a Breaking Point to be treated differently in terms of resolution as a general consideration. Mage does have special rules, but only for Conditions created by spells and mostly because of Mage's 'build your own spell' base line. The other 2e game lines do have magically created Conditions but if they're exceptions they're stated in those Conditions like any other Condition rather than assumed to be &quot;because magic.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:32:42-08:00","id":1023314,"title":"","content":"There's a reason I'm using generalities and &quot;rule of thumb.&quot; Because I know its not an official rule. In fact, the actual rules are very light, because hard rules get in the way when things do become important. However, understanding the point of view things come from helps a lot when addrssing issues, like the first poster's. <br /> <br /> If someone is twisting the rules in a way that doesn't make the game more fun for all involved, then something isn't right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-28-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:43:36-08:00","id":1023319,"title":"","content":"You can do scene long conditions if you want to. I don't personally agree that conditions should expire after just a scene (partly because I don't think people reboot every hour; I think day long conditions seems a lot more reasonable), but you can run your game however you like.<br /> My two points have been that scene long conditions is not an explicit rule, and that it's not the default way of handling conditions or otherwise the book wouldn't recommend handling it in a different manner.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry. Didn't see your post. I type very, very slowly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T10:08:58-08:00","id":1023330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1015611-spell-casting-and-the-inspired-condition-infinite-loop-question?p=1023319#post1023319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can do scene long conditions if you want to. I don't personally agree that conditions should expire after just a scene (partly because I don't think people reboot every hour; I think day long conditions seems a lot more reasonable), but you can run your game however you like.<br /> My two points have been that scene long conditions is not an explicit rule, and that it's not the default way of handling conditions or otherwise the book wouldn't recommend handling it in a different manner.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry. Didn't see your post. I type very, very slowly.</div> </div> </div> </div>A scene could be a day long, or 30 seconds of gun-slinging action. It's another thing that's loosely defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T10:14:10-08:00","id":1023332,"title":"","content":"Loosely defined but still implied. Hence in Advanced Spell Duration is has 1 hour/Scene. That isn't a set in stone definition but it is an implied length of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T10:24:44-08:00","id":1023335,"title":"","content":"Hour long scenes is another one of those &quot;rule of thumb&quot; things. Personally, I ignore that suggestion entirely. A scene should last exactly as long as it needs to for the purpose of dramatic pacing, and no longer or shorter. Keeping to that 1 hour guideline can only harm the pacing of a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}